A||N||5||Xtreme Fiero's||NOS kits||||5||
Z||000000||Xtreme Fiero's||10-25-2000||08:41 AM||||<BR>I was looking @ the Nitrous works universal 50/75/150 shot kit. What kind of power gains would I get in a Stock 2.8 (.30 over) only useing the 50 & 75 HP shots not the 150 for a while  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"> also what kind of 1/4 times could I expect? The NOS will only hold me over until I get a good turbo ket ready to go on.||||reg||5
Z||000001||1FST2M6||10-25-2000||08:59 AM||||the NOS kits are set to 50/70 hp with the STOCK pistons... you'll have to increase the nitrous fed to the motor if you in crease the displacment... (put our kit on a mustang yeas it's 70shot for us but it's a 45 shot for him) the stock jets are .036 and .042 change them to .040 and .040 you'll have higher fuel pressure and more nitrous. 1/4 times in the low 14s... with DOT slicks high to mid 13s. what tranny are you using? and fighting wheel hop will be a factor... well it was for me. Shaun41178 seems to have tamed it. once the turbos are on run a RPM limited 40ish shot to help the turbos spool up faster. have it shut off at 2500-3000rpm. <A HREF="http://www.nosnitrous.com" TARGET=_blank>www.nosnitrous.com</A>  #05120  or <A HREF="http://www.nitrousworks.com" TARGET=_blank>www.nitrousworks.com</A>  #13093  make SURE your fuel pump is in good working order and that you injectors are clean.. if your on an emission controlled car plan on replacing the cat in a few months.. the heat will TRASH it. <P>------------------<BR>Shhh.. Top Secret! <BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/1fstcheeto_2.jpg">  <p>[This message has been edited by 1FST2M6 (edited 10-25-2000).]||||reg||1
Z||000002||TheFiero64||10-25-2000||11:21 AM||||Hey Xtreme Fiero's, Didn't you have enough of a disaster blowing up Iron dukes with NOS?<BR>lol<P>------------------<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/TheFiero64_signature1.gif"> ||||reg||1
Z||000003||Shaun41178||10-25-2000||12:52 PM||||Yea I don't have much wheel hop but I also have an auto tranny which seems to help in that department.  My belief is that the torque converter helps limit the amount of power to the wheels.   Good for launching but not good for top end as I fall on my face in that dept.  Most likely if I went to a higher stall TC I might get some wheel hop but not sure.<P>A 36 nitrous and a 42 bypass will still probably give close to a 70 hp jump.  A .030 over 2.8 doesn't have that much of a displacment increase to really bring down the power.  It might be more like a 65 shot.  I wouldn't go higher then a 40 nitrous jet though.  That could be pushing the limits of your 2.8<P>Also make sure you have a new fuel filter.  If it is dirty at all you run the risk of leaning out top end.  I had 30k miles on my filter, 4 years old.  I just replaced it last month and on the nitrous I could tell it was pulling better top end.  I didn't have detonation anymore either as I had when I went to the track about 2 months ago.<P>I don't know the condition of my cat but as fat as I can tell it still seams to be in good working order.  I don't hear any rattling and it doesn't seem to be choking my car at all.  However if you live in a state without smog check or visual inspections I would just say to remove it or gut it.  The cat hurts top end and really chokes the engine top end especially on the nitrous.<P>Depending on your tranny and your driving capabilities I would say you should easily run 14's.  With practice launching and good tuning, I think it is possible to get into the 13's.  Tranny is a big factor and an auto will be more consistent but a manual will ger you down the track faster unless of course you don't shift to fastly.  No offense as I dont' know if you can its just that not all people are as good at it as others.  i think the nitrous kit will hold you over for quite a long time.<P>Hey Travis I was hoping you could take a look at my dyno graphs.  I was thinking of replacing my 42 bypass with a 40 bypass.  I don't know if I am running lean top end or if the bottle pressure is just getting lower as I go further down the track/higher load.  I know I could hit the dyno and see if there is any improvement but at $75 for two dyno pulls and my limited budget right now I would just rather ask you to see what you found out from doing that.  How much does it actually raise pressure at the rail and should I worry about locking up the injectors?  what abut going to a 38 bypass?  I still have the stock injectors and stock FPR.  I just seems that after about 4k the power drops off almost to like n/a conditions as the graph shows.  I don't know maybe it is just the cam I have in it that has no power top end?  You can just email me if you prefer.  Thanks.<P>------------------<BR>Shaun-Toledo OH, 85 GT<BR>3.2 With nitrous<BR>http://members.aol.com/shaun41178||||reg||1
Z||000004||1FST2M6||10-25-2000||03:12 PM||||if you have a 38 DROP IT IN!  10-12psi is what we saw on the dyno(over the supplied 42)... (screw in fuel pressure guage) just ground the pressure sensor and POOF your set. and the more fuel the better. we had problems making my fuel actually work right.. it would dead head the pump HEAT it up and the pressure would lock the valve in the RC injector?!? RC SWORE that can't happen.. but the shop was able to re-create it on a flow bench.  (120+psi)  <P>thats why i went to the AUTO.. less to worry about no missed shifts, no failing clutches (5) and equal length shafts so no torque steer and for all you that say theres no such thing as torque steer in a rwd car drive a fiero 4spd with nitrous.. it'll change lanes like a van in the wind! I'm sure the V8 cars do to.<P>the cams on our cars SUCK! don't expect much out of it after 4500.. even at 7000 it's suckin wind and wasting more fuel then its burning.. valves complain, and it ticks and pops for 1/2 hours after the run.. but ALWAYS starts right back up and ready to go again! $75 for 2 pulls is a lot! our friend/club discount is $50 for 3 normal rate is $65 for 3!  NITROUS IS COOL! My cat self-dectructed... there was NOTHING left inside.. no ratteling, not complaining.. just EMPTY.. and the Guys a Random Tech. said "thats not covered under warranty" but in their literature it state "ok for use in Nitrous fed vehicles" oh well it passed emission when i needed it to... humm..  i need another kit... ... ...<P>------------------<BR>Shhh.. Top Secret! <BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/1fstcheeto_2.jpg"> ||||reg||1
Z||000005||JohnnyK||10-25-2000||04:04 PM||||Yeah, shouldnt you already HAVE a NOS kit?  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">||||reg||1
